id: E2181
draft: true
title: "旧版 Autotools GNU 归档的 OHOS 三元组与 Windows 挂载权限边界"
category: autotools, ohos, cross-build, permissions, validation
match_keywords: >
  aarch64-linux-ohos config.sub, config.guess HarmonyOS, Autotools cross configure,
  C compiler cannot create executables, Windows mounted filesystem chmod,
  HMDFS umask, target executable staging
root_cause: >
  GNU release tarballs often ship config.guess/config.sub snapshots that predate
  the linux-ohos triplet. A cross configure therefore rejects a valid OHOS host
  before compilation. Separately, running POSIX permission tests on a Windows
  mounted source or staging tree can report mode 0777 for every file and make
  delayed-setstat tests fail even though the same build passes on a native POSIX
  filesystem. These are independent boundaries and must not be conflated.
error_signature: >
  Invalid configuration .*ohos.*not recognized|C compiler cannot create executables|
  expected mode 700|expected mode 500|all tests were successful on POSIX but
  chmod results are 0777 on /mnt/*
trigger_tool: autotools, conan, clang, w3-validator
phase: source-prepare, configure, build, upstream-test, target-staging
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Bind the target triplet before configure by adding only the OHOS recognition
  rules required by the checked-in helpers, and replace generated configure
  temporary-directory umask 077 only where the target filesystem requires it.
  Run permission-sensitive upstream tests on a native POSIX scratch filesystem,
  while keeping source, recipe, and evidence hashes under the task root. For
  target validation, stage the exact AArch64 ELF outputs, verify NEEDED closure,
  sign on the target with the native self-sign tool, and execute one consumer
  round-trip.
rec_command: >
  patch config.guess/config.sub before ./configure --host=aarch64-linux-ohos;
  configure and make with the OHOS SDK; run make -C tests check on POSIX;
  inspect llvm-readelf -h/-d; sign and run cpio create/extract on the target
verification_cmd: >
  require configure success, target Machine=AArch64, NEEDED={libc.so}, upstream
  test denominator 17/17, consumer assertions 6/6, and target run output
  W3_RESULT=PASS bound to the same payload SHA and transaction receipt chain
affected_scope: >
  Autotools C command-line tools whose source archives include generated GNU
  portability helpers and whose tests assert Unix mode bits. The POSIX scratch
  rule applies only to host-side test evidence; it does not waive target
  execution, signing, transfer, or release gates.
safety_boundary: >
  Do not replace an invalid source/version with a nearby release, do not treat
  recipe-only graph success as an OHOS binary, and do not claim target PASS from
  host tests. Keep the original archive immutable, use a task-private staging
  root, and never relaunch a consumed W3 transaction after a signing or payload
  change.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E2181-draft-2301_80739235.md
last_updated: 2026-09-09
